# 1️⃣ Database Security Basics

## Big Idea

Database security means:

```text
Protect data from:
• Unauthorized access
• Data leaks
• Data modification
• Data loss
```

---

## Mental Model 🧠

Think of a college.

Not everyone can access everything.

### Student

Can:

✔ View marks

Cannot:

❌ Change marks

---

### Teacher

Can:

✔ Update marks

Cannot:

❌ Access payroll data

---

### Principal

Can:

✔ Access everything

---

Databases work exactly like this.

---

# Why Security Matters

Suppose table:

| id | name   | salary |
| -- | ------ | ------ |
| 1  | Akshay | 50000  |

If every employee can run:

```sql
SELECT * FROM employees;
```

Sensitive salary data becomes exposed.

---

# Security Goals

---

## 🔹 Confidentiality

Only authorized people see data.

---

Example:

```text
HR → Salary Data ✔

Student → Salary Data ❌
```

---

## 🔹 Integrity

Data remains correct.

Nobody can modify it improperly.

---

Example:

```text
Marks = 90

Unauthorized user changes to 100 ❌
```

---

## 🔹 Availability

Authorized users can access data when needed.

---

Memory Trick:

```text
CIA

Confidentiality
Integrity
Availability
```

---

# Common Security Threats

---

## SQL Injection

Very famous interview topic.

Bad code:

```python
query = "SELECT * FROM users WHERE name='" + user_input + "'"
```

Attacker enters:

```text
' OR '1'='1
```

Query becomes dangerous.

---

Solution:

```python
Use parameterized queries
```

Never concatenate user input directly.

